; The Media Foundation imports waaudio.dll links against.
;
; Why a .def and not `Mfplat.lib`: the import library that ships with Kits 10 for
; ARM names `Mfplat.dll`, which is what a desktop Windows image links against. The
; phone ships the module as `MFPlat.DLL` - that is the spelling `WhatsAppNative.dll`
; imports from - and a module name is copied verbatim into the import descriptor.
;
; Why exactly these four: on 6 November 2026 the phone answered 0x8007007F
; (procedure not found) to version 1, which imported `MFEnumDeviceSources` and the
; source reader. The seven functions this phone's MFPlat.DLL is proven to export are
; the ones WhatsAppNative.dll imports: MFStartup, MFShutdown, MFCreateSample,
; MFCreateMediaBufferWrapper, MFCreateAttributes, MFCreateMediaType and
; MFCreateMFByteStreamOnStream. The probe uses four of them.
LIBRARY MFPlat.dll

EXPORTS
    MFStartup
    MFShutdown
    MFCreateAttributes
    MFCreateMediaType
    MFCreateSample
